1
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:08,633
`workbench serve` prints a one-time sign-in link. Open it, and you're in
Single use, expires in 5 minutes, never sent to the server in a URL; no token to copy

2
00:00:08,633 --> 00:00:12,867
Home asks one question. Everything else is one step away
Genesis release P0 was installed and verified at setup

3
00:00:12,867 --> 00:00:17,567
Honest by default: this recording uses a deterministic fake model
Kernel, database, sandboxed builds, Lean proofs and release gates are all real

4
00:00:17,567 --> 00:00:20,067
System facts sit in one quiet line: checker, protected components, sandbox

5
00:00:20,067 --> 00:00:24,167
Run a real job: audit a package with build, proof and two reviews

6
00:00:24,167 --> 00:00:26,667
A job is pinned to the release that was active when it started
Steps show what each waits for and whose output it uses

7
00:00:26,667 --> 00:00:29,833
Pause stops new work; anything running settles first

8
00:00:29,833 --> 00:00:38,833
Each try shows five separate facts: allowed to run, what the machine saw, model call, result kept, cleanup
Time compressed 3×

9
00:00:38,833 --> 00:00:41,833
Paused: completed work is kept; this job stays on P0

10
00:00:41,833 --> 00:00:44,100
Now ask the workbench to improve its own orchestration

11
00:00:44,100 --> 00:00:48,667
A plain-language request, bound to the active release and a fixed budget

12
00:00:48,667 --> 00:00:50,133
Start: the current release (P0) writes and checks its own successor

13
00:00:50,133 --> 00:00:51,267
Every improvement shows where it is: requested, written, checked, published, approved, active
Codex (mocked) proposes exact file edits · time compressed 8×

14
00:00:51,267 --> 00:00:56,267
The first attempt had a real proof error — the fixed verifier rejected it
Lean's actual diagnostic is shown; no model can override it

15
00:00:56,267 --> 00:00:56,367
The diagnostic went back to the author as a recorded new draft; the second attempt is checked
Sandboxed build, proof replay, protected tests, two independent reviews · time compressed 10×

16
00:00:56,367 --> 00:01:02,367
What changes, in plain words: refute no longer waits for reproduce
No data dependency between them, so both may run at once; both gates are still required

17
00:01:02,367 --> 00:01:06,700
Publication waits until every required gate passes
Time compressed 10×

18
00:01:06,700 --> 00:01:10,667
Release P1 was published by the protected kernel. It's waiting for you

19
00:01:10,667 --> 00:01:15,567
The decision comes first: the exact release, what it replaces, and the evidence
Full digests, grouped for reading

20
00:01:15,567 --> 00:01:23,933
Each fact keeps its own label. There is no single 'verified' badge
Model reviews are judgments, not proofs, and here they are marked as mocked

21
00:01:23,933 --> 00:01:33,000
Details are one click away: every proof obligation, general or finite, re-checked from scratch

22
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:36,000
Activation never moves existing jobs: they stay on P0 unless explicitly migrated

23
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:46,333
Approve: type the release's first 8 characters and acknowledge the mocked reviews
Approval binds this exact digest to the current active release

24
00:01:46,333 --> 00:01:55,533
Activate is a separate step: a compare-and-swap on the expected active release

25
00:01:55,533 --> 00:02:02,633
P1 is now the default for new jobs; the paused job is still pinned to P0

26
00:02:02,633 --> 00:02:06,533
A new job runs on P1

27
00:02:06,533 --> 00:02:09,833
Build and proof run first…
Time compressed 10×

28
00:02:09,833 --> 00:02:14,533
…then reproduction and refutation run at the same time under P1
Both publication gates are still mandatory and bound to the same payload

29
00:02:14,533 --> 00:02:23,100
Both reviews passed; the summary step combines them

